{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>As much as they can carry:</b> More than what was owed to them for the money they had brought to him." "<b>And put every man's money in the mouth of his sack:</b> With their knowledge, for he said to them: 'My lord knows that he did you wrong and sought to do you good.' For if he had done this the first time without their knowledge, they would have had an excuse regarding the goblet — that what was done with it was as what was done with the money. But it was with their knowledge, and they recognized the money just as they recognized the grain, for they recognized that he had given them as much as they could carry. And if it had been without their knowledge, perhaps he could have charged against them that the money was also this time hidden, but this is impossible regarding the goblet, and who can contend with one mightier than himself. And know that because the providers were very numerous from all the land of Egypt, and many nations mingled within it, those who came would give their sacks and their money to the provider, and he would measure out to them according to the money found with them, and they would take what was given them, since the king's word is sovereign, and furthermore because he acts in good faith. Therefore the first time they took their sacks sealed and did not know what was inside them, and similarly the second time."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:23.532068803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}